[[:db/add "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3" :answer/id #uuid "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3"] [:db/add "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3" :answer/value "1"] [:db/ensure "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3" :answer/validate] [:db/add "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2"] [:db/add "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/choices "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3"] [:db/add "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/correct "d64f1855-c3ca-5fed-b957-c3a6098f05f3"] [:db/ensure "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/id #uuid "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f"] [:db/add "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/89/89ead421f6a93de9dd52418fa041a4b849d131ea89a87fb18c5f118326e60c57.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{3}{2}\\,(1, -1)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -\\frac{3}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(2, -4).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/54/5447bc67b11cfc569d5a04eb6e94164ada1fa82782ba423722a3c6bd01d70e4b.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{2}{2}=1 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=1$."] [:db/add "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/answer-fields "aa75cfd9-53e4-54ec-9da0-33f01ac8c0f2"] [:db/ensure "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "b9ef916c-2156-5854-8496-c6e069949f1f"] [:db/add "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848" :answer/id #uuid "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848"] [:db/add "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848" :answer/value "1"] [:db/ensure "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9"] [:db/add "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/choices "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848"] [:db/add "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/correct "de0da730-a340-51ed-8da9-2f1055c55848"] [:db/ensure "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/id #uuid "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d"] [:db/add "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/9b/9ba36afbf950658168bc518a816644c166d5ff5ab0a94211801e5671d31f3c11.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{3}{2}\\,(-2, -3)=\\left(-3, -\\frac{9}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-4, -2).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c6/c6b86b252674f7d90646938ae31c3a0da85d333d3bc85d39158b2797289748f8.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-2}{-2}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=1$."] [:db/add "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/answer-fields "a610d70d-b8a6-56a0-b23f-94f6ab69f0d9"] [:db/ensure "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d"] [:db/add "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed" :answer/id #uuid "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed"] [:db/add "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}"] [:db/ensure "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed" :answer/validate] [:db/add "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad"] [:db/add "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/choices "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed"] [:db/add "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/correct "2486725f-e9bc-591c-aab4-ecfd653eeaed"] [:db/ensure "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/id #uuid "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2"] [:db/add "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/65/65f1cf69502cf5650f9bface4f5bddd453b2abac588cba228aadb66806f27397.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(-1, 3)=\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-1, 1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/31/31a3b382de27d55a5ececfc928c4a57c3772af8031da56565f31c2d840a2943b.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, 4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-1}{-4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{4}$."] [:db/add "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/answer-fields "afe77219-9832-5832-a8a7-2e698c3996ad"] [:db/ensure "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2"] [:db/add "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42" :answer/id #uuid "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42"] [:db/add "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}"] [:db/ensure "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42" :answer/validate] [:db/add "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee"] [:db/add "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/choices "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42"] [:db/add "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/correct "a6f5c409-49a7-535a-aa12-44ac7f72db42"] [:db/ensure "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/id #uuid "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8"] [:db/add "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/ba/baa813bfb835f8d56faf0fbbf33de2710d6aa4d2f08e1c8c0038bb3124c34cf3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(3, 1)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/9d/9de04a873bbf94f85e2d53a0afec52a1c9c78ee6f4f8f748f2402f35bd0dad4c.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, 2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{2}=\\frac{5}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{2}=\\frac{5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{5}{4}$."] [:db/add "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/answer-fields "3baac245-5544-58cc-846c-f99e98da09ee"] [:db/ensure "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8"] [:db/add "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615" :answer/id #uuid "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615"] [:db/add "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] [:db/ensure "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615" :answer/validate] [:db/add "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015"] [:db/add "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/choices "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615"] [:db/add "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/correct "ce57800f-849e-5f61-b11e-45ff3128b615"] [:db/ensure "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/id #uuid "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c"] [:db/add "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/5d/5de299a8b3d58c9a0b5272e9f5ed9e8af52fc47d5e6f5167c3864d437ec9a5ea.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{3}{2}\\,(-2, 1)=\\left(-3, \\frac{3}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-1, 1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b1/b1a2796e7ce9f104c863ed52bf7d79c577ecfc02cabfa624401154f35a8aa1db.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-1}{-2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}$."] [:db/add "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/answer-fields "2a4f54e1-0c03-5106-b316-4d5bc0c11015"] [:db/ensure "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "ee44a393-26e5-5a8c-a2ca-add9fd4d552c"] [:db/add "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d" :answer/id #uuid "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d"] [:db/add "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] [:db/ensure "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d" :answer/validate] [:db/add "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99"] [:db/add "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/choices "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d"] [:db/add "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/correct "115dacd0-f58c-5f6f-990e-ec8435284c8d"] [:db/ensure "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/id #uuid "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be"] [:db/add "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/dd/dd759f3e9127fccdf2f2ec70f72574888319844368ae1d7ad9e2088948092b2a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\,(1, 1)=\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(1, 2).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/13/133edd8147d930d3ad98473e06db0121fe43ca2ea91870a4ff91470db3dafcbf.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, 4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}$."] [:db/add "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/answer-fields "5e05df3d-eca7-569d-b77d-742487dd1e99"] [:db/ensure "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be"] [:db/add "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419" :answer/id #uuid "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419"] [:db/add "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}"] [:db/ensure "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3"] [:db/add "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/choices "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419"] [:db/add "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/correct "635fd841-a592-5efb-8f31-d2181d54a419"] [:db/ensure "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/id #uuid "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4"] [:db/add "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/a5/a5ed245562242fd0250788abba50ad1590d135c370df6ca859f4c685de025969.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(-3, -1)=\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}, -\\frac{1}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}, -\\frac{7}{2}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f3/f34061f5ffb1c2aaab8728cb51f3dc88df57e1c483e2fae478eb659c220284d2.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{7}{4}$."] [:db/add "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/answer-fields "4506d7df-28f8-57fd-9049-0b569b5e9ce3"] [:db/ensure "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4"] [:db/add "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5" :answer/id #uuid "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5"] [:db/add "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5" :answer/value "2"] [:db/ensure "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5" :answer/validate] [:db/add "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b"] [:db/add "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/choices "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5"] [:db/add "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/correct "cd140002-9cb8-552b-9fd0-71608721a2f5"] [:db/ensure "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/id #uuid "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29"] [:db/add "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/6b/6b053cd19e77620430bfbeb259117c965ce2420455de9363db687f02f6f142d4.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\,(2, -3)=\\left(5, -\\frac{15}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(4, -8).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/13/13b64631f34fdd5cc14f6c14e02de127f40bcea8232f1e3ef191fe07a77403e8.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{4}{2}=2 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-8}{-4}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."] [:db/add "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/answer-fields "42fcc497-c469-5514-8093-4d331bbd3e9b"] [:db/ensure "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29"] [:db/ensure 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/validate]]
